 Contemporaneous association is not six-hour predictive contribution, and a rank-partial association does not demonstrate a causal effect or a gain in model performance. The candidate-pool dependence and matched C6 results in Section~\ref{sec:predictor_selection_results} therefore qualify the original screening rationale. A separate, pre-specified q21 configuration, C3, added upstream U1 inputs (the original seven variables plus ws, averaged over 52.75--53.75$^\circ$N, 10.5--7.0$^\circ$W) and U2 inputs (500-hPa geopotential and total-column water vapour, cosine-latitude weighted over 50--57$^\circ$N, 20--7$^\circ$W). Overall RMSE decreased by 6.4\% for XGBoost and 7.0\% for BiLSTM-Attention. C3 expands both spatial coverage and the predictor count from seven to 17, so it is not a controlled seven-variable selection comparison. C3a (U1 only, 15 predictors) and C3b (U2 only, nine predictors) were added after inspecting C3 and are exploratory. Their results are reported separately in Supplementary Tables~\ref{supp-stab:r2m3_upstream_xgboost} and~\ref{supp-stab:r2m3_upstream_bilstm_attn}. These spatial sensitivity tests show that the local configuration can omit useful upstream information; they do not establish a uniquely best selection strategy.
